      "content": "can we focus on the technical side though? i'm not sure what you mean by \"goblin shadows\" in a networking context. specifically, if we're looking at deep packet inspection (DPI) to catch these anomalies, what kind of specific signatures or heuristic patterns should we be looking for to differentiate between a legitimate automated spike (like a cron job or a backup) and a malicious actor trying to hide their footprint?",
      "source": "evaluator"
